  "img": "modules/dnd-players-handbook/assets/icons/items/scimitar.webp",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>A slender, fey-forged scimitar, its curve chased with gold that catches a light not quite there. It was the blade of a duelist of the fey roads, said never to have cut an innocent — who came south into the Misty Forest a century ago on the trail of a story every seeker since has followed: a relic of great power, shattered into four pieces and scattered through the wilds. Like all the others, the duelist did not come out. The blade was lost with its bearer to the webs of a hidden temple, and has lain dormant ever since, its old dawn waiting on a worthy hand.</p><p>To such a hand its fey magic stirs: once between dawns it yields a cluster of dew-bright berries; once between dawns it throws off a bloom of clinging faerie light that lets nothing hide in shadow.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
    "price": {
      "value": 4000,
      "denomination": "gp"
    },
